course: dictionary
lesson: 13279
title: Governed: ruled or controlled
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Govern means to rule or to control. When you add -ed, it becomes governed, which tells you something was ruled or controlled in the past. «The country was governed by a wise queen.» The queen ruled the country, so governed means ruled.
explain: Governed can also be used as a describing word. «The governed» means the people who are ruled. In a kingdom, the king governs, and the people are the governed. You can say it in a sentence too: «The governed people paid their taxes.»
explain: Scientists use governed in a different way. «The planets move in paths governed by gravity.» Here governed means controlled by a law. The paths are not random: they follow the rules of gravity. Games work the same way, as in «The game is governed by strict rules.»
fact: Govern means to rule or to control.
fact: Governed is the past of govern, and it means ruled or controlled.
fact: «The governed» means the people who are ruled.
fact: «The game is governed by rules» means the rules control how the game is played.
fact: To check a meaning, swap in ruled or controlled and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The country was governed by a wise queen.» What does governed mean here? | *ruled or controlled | ruled | forgotten | painted
exercise: «The game is governed by rules that everyone must follow.» What controls the game? | The scoreboard | *The rules | The weather | Hungry players
exercise: Find and copy the word that means controlled by a law: «The planets move in paths governed by gravity.» | gravity | *governed | planets | paths
test: «Our class is governed by a school council.» What does governed mean? | celebrated | written down | ignored | *ruled or controlled
test: In a kingdom, who are the governed? | The king alone | The royal horses | *The people who are ruled | The castle walls
exam: Which sentence uses governed to mean ruled or controlled? | *The kingdom was governed by a wise king | The pencil governed the paper | She governed a big lunch | The hikers governed a map
